.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 22, 2026
.Dt DEVD.CONF 5
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm devd.conf
.Nd device event rules
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Ic on Ar verb class handler Oo Ar name Ns = Ns Ar pattern | name Ns != Ns Ar pattern ... Oc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Xr devd 8 Ns 's
configuration is a script in the language of
.Xr sh 1 ,
run when
.Nm devd
starts by a shell built into it: functions, variables,
.Ic case ,
.Ic \&.
and everything else sh has are there.
.Pa /etc/devd.conf
runs first, then every
.Pa *.conf
file in
.Pa /etc/devd
and then in
.Pa /usr/local/etc/devd ,
in lexical order, all in the one shell: a later file may call an earlier one's
functions.
.Ic exit
ends the file it is in.
.Pp
The shell has one command more:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic on Ar verb class handler Oo Ar name Ns = Ns Ar pattern | name Ns != Ns Ar pattern ... Oc
Adds a rule.
An event, as
.Xr devctl 4
describes them, matches it when its verb matches
.Ar verb ,
its class
.Ar class ,
and every condition holds:
.Ar name Ns = Ns Ar pattern
when the event has field
.Ar name
and its value matches
.Ar pattern ,
.Ar name Ns != Ns Ar pattern
when it has no such field or the value doesn't match.
.Ar verb ,
.Ar class
and each
.Ar pattern
are patterns as
.Ic case
reads them
.Po
.Ql * ,
.Ql \&? ,
.Ql [...] ;
a backslash makes the next character plain
.Pc ,
so quote them to keep the shell from expanding them as file names.
.Ar handler
is shell text, run as
.Ic eval
runs it: a function's name, or a command line in quotes.
.El
.Pp
For each event, every rule it matches runs, in the order
.Ic on
added them, in a child process of
.Nm devd
in which the variables
.Va verb ,
.Va class
and one for each of the event's fields
.Po
.Va name ,
.Va bus ,
.Va model ...
.Pc
hold its values, exported to the commands the handler runs.
The values are the device's, never shell text: a handler that quotes them
.Pq Ql \&"$model\&"
is safe from anything a device reports.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /usr/local/etc/devd/*.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/devd.conf
.It Pa /etc/devd/*.conf
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/devd/*.conf
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
The stock
.Pa /etc/devd.conf
logs each drive attached or detached:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
on attach disk 'logger -t devd "disk $name attached: $model ($bus, $kind)"'
on detach disk 'logger -t devd "disk $name detached"'
.Ed
.Pp
and mounts a CD's disc, read-only, on the first
.Pa /cdrom/disk Ns Ar N
nothing is mounted on:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cd_mount()
{
	grep -q "^/dev/$name " /proc/mounts && return 0
	_n=0
	while grep -q " /cdrom/disk$_n " /proc/mounts; do
		_n=$((_n + 1))
	done
	mkdir -p "/cdrom/disk$_n" &&
	mount -t cd9660 -o ro "/dev/$name" "/cdrom/disk$_n"
}
on media cd cd_mount state=inserted
.Ed
.Pp
Every event but the
.Pa /dev
nodes', to the log:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
on '*' '*' 'logger -t devd "$verb $class $name"' class!=dev
.Ed
.Pp
Only drives on AHCI controllers other than the first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
on attach disk sata_drive bus=ahci 'controller!=0'
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr sh 1 ,
.Xr devctl 4 ,
.Xr devd 8
